    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d547">

                <pb facs="0660" n="1494" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1494"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/482</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Garrett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-22T19:00:00+01:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 22, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 23, 8.37 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2828. I had an informal conversation with the Minister for Foreign Affairs today
                    on the subject of your 1222, May 20, 6 p.m. He says he will consult his experts
                    and let me know in a day or two as definitely as he can when Dutch ships may be
                    expected to arrive to lift grain. He added that Gevers<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d547-f1"/> informed him this morning from Berlin that the two ships
                    to replace <hi rendition="#italic">Juno</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stella</hi> would probably get German permits without trouble, and Loudon
                    professes to be only waiting to hear from Beaufort that <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Juno</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Stella</hi> have received their
                    clearance papers before despatching these replacing ships. This also applied to
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Frisia</hi>, which I learn from another source is to
                    replace <hi rendition="#italic">Hollandia</hi>. See your 1170, May 8, 6
                        p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d547-f2"/> Loudon intimated that Germany is making
                    conditions which will prevent the despatch of more than a few Dutch ships.</p>
                <p>Could you advise me how soon <hi rendition="#italic">Juno</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stella</hi> are expected to leave?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
